-- No partisan politics in Vegans Explore news (Sean, 2026-10-31; canon canon-ve-news-nonpartisan). Applied the same day.
update lesaruss_dispatch_sources set instructions = instructions || E'\n\nNo partisan politics (Sean, 2026-10-31: "nothing controversial. Let''s stay away from Trump. Let''s stay away from politics if possible. Legislation is good... anything fighting for animal rights... if there''s something happening in Washington, D.C. that may be impacting the animals, Congress, that stuff is fine. But... Trump mispronounces vegan, let''s not go that route, because there''s a lot of vegans that are Republicans, and I don''t want to alienate our audience"). Vegans Explore is for every Vegan, whatever their politics. Never use a story about a politician, a party or an election for its own sake (gaffes, feuds, campaign news, what a politician said about Vegans), and never take a side. Bills, laws, rulings, regulations and agency actions that affect animals, food or Vegans are welcome: say what the law or ruling does and who it affects, in neutral words, naming a politician only as the bill''s sponsor or the official who acted. When in doubt, leave it out.',
 notes = coalesce(notes,'') || E'\n2026-10-31: No partisan politics (Sean).'
where key='pulse_topic_write' and instructions not like '%No partisan politics (Sean, 2026-10-31%';
